# =============================================================================
# .gitignore of iBuilder
#
# Three goals, in this order:
#   1. NEVER let a secret, a key, a certificate, a game file or a file derived from a game be committed by accident
#      (section 6 and 7). The project ships none of them and never will.
#   2. Keep build output and local artefacts out of the repository (sections 1 to 5).
#   3. Keep every tracked TEST FIXTURE trackable (section 8). The fixtures are synthetic and small; several of them
#      carry names that the rules above would otherwise hide (`*.nso`, `main`, `games/`, `bin/`, `shaders/`).
#
# How the rules are kept narrow: a generic directory name (`bin/`, `obj/`, `games/`, `shaders/`, `dist/`, `tmp/`,
# `Documents/`) is anchored with a leading slash (repository root) or to a named parent, never written bare, because
# `crates/*/src/bin/`, `docs/shaders/` and `crates/ibuilder-shadersplit/tests/data/games/` are real source folders.
# Only names that exist for one reason (`ExeFS/`, `extract/`, `shadercache/`, `.diag/`, `*.keys`, `*.p12`) are unanchored.
# A later rule wins over an earlier one: the re-inclusions (`!`) of section 8 must stay at the end.
# Verify after any change with:   git status --ignored   and   git ls-files --others --ignored --exclude-standard
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Rust / Cargo
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `Cargo.lock` stays TRACKED on purpose: the workspace builds binaries and a static library for the app.
target/
/target-*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
perf.data
perf.data.*
flamegraph*.svg


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Build output and local artefacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `scripts/build-app.sh` writes the IPA, its checksum and the manifests into dist/ (and the work tree into target/);
# `scripts/build-host.sh` writes the rebuilt engine host into dist/host/. All of it is output, not source.
/dist/
*.ipa
*.ipa.sha256
*.dylib
*.a
*.o
*.xcarchive
*.xcframework
*.framework
*.dSYM
*.app
*.nxgame
*.patched.bin
# leftovers of `patch` (scripts/check-patches-apply.sh and scripts/build-app.sh apply app/patches and engine-patches)
*.orig
*.rej

# .NET (the iOS app of app/ is built by `dotnet publish`; Rust's `src/bin/` is NOT touched: the rules are anchored)
/app/**/bin/
/app/**/obj/
/bin/
/obj/
/.dotnet/
/.nuget/
*.nupkg
*.binlog

# Xcode
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. macOS, editors, IDEs, agents
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.history/
# local state of coding agents and personal notes
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md
# scratch space
/tmp/
/scratch/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Logs and diagnostics (what a phone or a Mac run leaves behind)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The hidden diagnostics folder of the app (docs/DIAGNOSTICS.md) and anything pulled from a phone's container.
# These files contain paths, device names and timings: never commit one by accident.
*.log
*.stage
# stray tool output (a redirected cargo error once landed at the root as meta.err)
*.err
gameapp.*.log
.diag/
/Documents/
# crash reports and Instruments / Xcode result bundles
*.ips
*.crash
*.trace
*.xcresult


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Python (the oracle and measurement tools under crates/*/tools/ run on a Mac)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
fontvenv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. SECRETS and signing material: never committed, never published
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console keys
prod.keys
title.keys
*.keys
# Certificates, private keys, provisioning (the app imports them on the phone; they do not belong in a repository)
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.csr
*.certSigningRequest
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
ALTCertificate.p12
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
# Environment and credential files. The template stays tracked: scripts/local.env.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.toml
secrets.env
secrets.txt
*.secret
*.secrets
/scripts/local.env


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. GAME-DERIVED and CONSOLE-DERIVED files: never committed (no dump, no firmware, no font, no shader)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Containers and content (Switch and Switch 2)
*.nsp
*.xci
*.xcz
*.nsz
*.ncz
*.nup
*.nca
*.nacp
*.tik
*.nso
*.nro
*.npdm
*.romfs
RomFS.img
# A dump or an extraction folder. `ExeFS/` and `extract/` exist for no other reason; the loose module names are
# anchored to the repository root so they cannot hide a fixture called `main` (see section 8).
ExeFS/
extract/
/main
/sdk
/subsdk[0-9]
/rtld
/firmware/
/Firmware/
/out/
/out-*/
/games/
# Output of the rewriter and of the shader chain (they are the game's code and shaders, transformed)
*.fixups.tsv
*.sites.tsv
*.gates.tsv
*.cuts.tsv
*.obs.tsv
*.changed.tsv
*.match.tsv
*.dmsb
*.spv
*.metallib
shadercache/
/shaders/
**/shaders/*.work
# Saves
*.sav
# Fonts. The console's shared fonts are Nintendo's, macOS's Arial Unicode and Arial Rounded Bold are proprietary:
# no font file is tracked (NOTICE.md, "Fonts"). If a freely licensed font is added on purpose, re-include it by name.
*.bfttf
*.bfotf
*.ttf
*.otf
*.ttc
*.woff
*.woff2


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. RE-INCLUSIONS: the repository's own fixtures stay trackable
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The synthetic NSO modules of ibuilder-rewrite (crates/ibuilder-rewrite/tests/fixtures/{select,stubs,synth}/*.nso)
# are small hand-made files, not game modules. Only the fixture folders of a crate are re-included, so a real NSO
# anywhere else (for example next to the sources) stays ignored.
!/crates/*/tests/fixtures/**/*.nso
!/crates/*/tests/data/**/*.nso
# the synthetic NROs of the shader splitter's CRA games (tests/data/games/sync-cra*/nro: the module a CRA archive's file table is in)
!/crates/*/tests/data/**/*.nro
# a future fixture that mimics a dump folder
!/crates/*/tests/**/ExeFS/
